WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.442
The assessment starter asks for one row per product and month.

00:00:03.442 --> 00:00:08.307
The browser version is already complete so you can run it and inspect the result.

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:14.357
In a student assignment, you can remove part of the SELECT or GROUP BY and ask students to finish it.

00:00:14.357 --> 00:00:20.842
After running it, explain the output grain and why a Spark version may need a shuffle for the grouping keys.

00:00:20.842 --> 00:00:24.707
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:24.707 --> 00:00:29.552
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:29.552 --> 00:00:32.872
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:32.872 --> 00:00:36.812
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:36.812 --> 00:00:43.147
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:43.147 --> 00:00:48.772
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project: validate the meaning of the result,

00:00:48.772 --> 00:00:50.926
not only whether the statement executes.
